1
00:00:03,277 --> 00:00:13,641
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this is Majjhima Nikāya 152, the development of the faculties, indriya, bhāvan, sūtra.

2
00:00:14,161 --> 00:00:22,745
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it says, on one occasion, the Blessed One was living at Khajangala, in a grove of Mukhera trees.

3
00:00:23,605 --> 00:00:30,868
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, the Brahmin student Uttara, a pupil of the Brahmin Parasārya, went to the Blessed One, exchanged greetings with him.

4
00:00:33,123 --> 00:00:41,306
[SPEAKER_00]: The best one then asked him, Uttara, does the Brahman, Parasārya, teach his disciples the development of the faculties?

5
00:00:42,266 --> 00:00:43,547
[SPEAKER_00]: He does, Master Gautama.

6
00:00:44,527 --> 00:00:48,149
[SPEAKER_00]: But, Uttara, how does he teach his disciples the development of the faculties?

7
00:00:49,409 --> 00:00:55,171
[SPEAKER_00]: Here, Master Gautama, one does not see forms with the eye, one does not hear sounds with the ear.

8
00:00:55,912 --> 00:01:01,854
[SPEAKER_00]: That is how the Brahman, Parasārya, teaches his disciples the development of the faculties.

9
00:01:03,127 --> 00:01:09,831
[SPEAKER_00]: And the Buddha says, well, if that is so, Uttara, then a blind man and a deaf man will have developed faculties.

10
00:01:11,312 --> 00:01:11,712
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

11
00:01:12,933 --> 00:01:13,953
[SPEAKER_01]: According to what?

12
00:01:14,154 --> 00:01:17,956
[SPEAKER_01]: Impair your senses and you'll be accomplished in that.

13
00:01:21,238 --> 00:01:29,823
[SPEAKER_00]: And so, when this was said, the Brahmin student, Uttara, sat silent, dismayed, depressed, without a response.

14
00:01:32,475 --> 00:01:35,096
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, knowing this, the Blessed One addressed the Venerable Ananda.

15
00:01:35,416 --> 00:01:45,259
[SPEAKER_00]: Ananda, the Brahmin Padasārya, teaches his disciples the development of the faculties in one way, but in the Noble One's discipline, the supreme development of the faculties is otherwise.

16
00:01:47,339 --> 00:01:49,400
[SPEAKER_00]: Ananda says, now is the time to...

17
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:51,281
[SPEAKER_00]: He asked the Buddha to explain.

18
00:01:53,981 --> 00:01:59,103
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, now, Ananda, how is there the supreme development of the faculties in the Noble One's discipline?

19
00:02:00,483 --> 00:02:02,004
[SPEAKER_00]: Here, Ananda, when a bhikkhu,

20
00:02:03,329 --> 00:02:04,930
[SPEAKER_00]: And the Pali is just bhikkhu there.

21
00:02:06,570 --> 00:02:06,850
[SPEAKER_01]: What?

22
00:02:06,910 --> 00:02:07,751
[SPEAKER_01]: Noble one's discipline.

23
00:02:08,111 --> 00:02:09,492
[SPEAKER_00]: Noble one's discipline, yeah.

24
00:02:09,572 --> 00:02:11,072
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's already this sort of an opinion.

25
00:02:11,652 --> 00:02:12,893
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, I want to point that out.

26
00:02:13,093 --> 00:02:17,915
[SPEAKER_00]: It's, yeah, noble one's discipline, but then he refers to a bhikkhu.

27
00:02:18,135 --> 00:02:18,535
[SPEAKER_01]: Sure.

28
00:02:21,036 --> 00:02:23,097
[SPEAKER_00]: A bhikkhu sees a form with the eye.

29
00:02:24,237 --> 00:02:32,821
[SPEAKER_00]: There arises in him what is agreeable, or to say, there arises what is disagreeable, there arises what is both agreeable and disagreeable.

30
00:02:34,255 --> 00:02:35,395
[SPEAKER_00]: He understands thus.

31
00:02:36,055 --> 00:02:43,097
[SPEAKER_00]: There hasn't arisen in me what is agreeable, what is... or what is disagreeable, or what is both agreeable and disagreeable.

32
00:02:44,078 --> 00:02:51,039
[SPEAKER_00]: But that is determined, gross, or... and dependently arisen.

33
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:52,020
[SPEAKER_00]: Gross?

34
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:52,500
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't know.

35
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:54,140
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just... Not subtle.

36
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:55,461
[SPEAKER_00]: Not... yeah.

37
00:02:55,601 --> 00:02:56,721
[SPEAKER_00]: Or... or lārikāṃ.

38
00:02:57,261 --> 00:02:57,561
[SPEAKER_00]: Right.

39
00:02:57,581 --> 00:02:57,801
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

40
00:02:58,281 --> 00:03:00,022
[SPEAKER_01]: Not like gross or disgusting.

41
00:03:00,082 --> 00:03:00,202
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

42
00:03:00,222 --> 00:03:00,802
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not subtle.

43
00:03:02,685 --> 00:03:04,706
[SPEAKER_00]: It is determined, dependently arisen.

44
00:03:05,546 --> 00:03:08,327
[SPEAKER_00]: This is peaceful, this is sublime, this is equanimity.

45
00:03:09,447 --> 00:03:18,429
[SPEAKER_00]: The agreeable that arose, the disagreeable that arose, and both the agreeable and disagreeable that arose, cease in him, and equanimity is established.

46
00:03:20,510 --> 00:03:21,010
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this is...

47
00:03:23,011 --> 00:03:24,671
[SPEAKER_01]: It's, yeah, it's what we mentioned before, of course.

48
00:03:24,711 --> 00:03:31,093
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not about avoiding or trying to get rid of the sights, agreeable or disagreeable ones, by going beyond them.

49
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:37,422
[SPEAKER_01]: But, you go beyond them, not by developing new sights that you haven't seen before.

50
00:03:38,062 --> 00:03:41,483
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, like when people say, oh, you get into meditation, then you see things that you don't see.

51
00:03:42,043 --> 00:03:44,124
[SPEAKER_01]: As in, you actually perceive things that you don't perceive.

52
00:03:44,204 --> 00:03:44,364
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

53
00:03:45,365 --> 00:03:49,146
[SPEAKER_01]: You develop meditation, you understand the nature of your sights.

54
00:03:49,446 --> 00:03:50,547
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how you go beyond them.

55
00:03:52,067 --> 00:03:54,348
[SPEAKER_01]: And nature, Pali word for nature is dhamma.

56
00:03:55,568 --> 00:03:57,009
[SPEAKER_00]: Pali word for things, it's dhamma.

57
00:03:57,669 --> 00:03:59,690
[SPEAKER_00]: Understanding dhamma means understanding things.

58
00:04:00,431 --> 00:04:01,932
[SPEAKER_00]: This thing is dependently arisen.

59
00:04:01,972 --> 00:04:02,512
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, exactly.

60
00:04:02,572 --> 00:04:05,773
[SPEAKER_01]: He understands that it has nothing to do with him.

61
00:04:06,113 --> 00:04:07,154
[SPEAKER_01]: He's dependently arisen.

62
00:04:07,534 --> 00:04:09,935
[SPEAKER_01]: It's another way of saying he's arisen independent of me.

63
00:04:12,016 --> 00:04:13,696
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not arisen for me.

64
00:04:14,176 --> 00:04:16,657
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not arisen from my essence of I am.

65
00:04:17,278 --> 00:04:18,338
[SPEAKER_01]: I am not its creator.

66
00:04:19,298 --> 00:04:25,661
[SPEAKER_01]: A noble disciple, in a discipline of one, all they need to do is remind themselves of that whenever things arise and they'll become an arahant.

67
00:04:31,222 --> 00:04:33,243
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is exactly what Mūla Parīhā Sūtra said.

68
00:04:33,724 --> 00:04:33,964
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

69
00:04:35,164 --> 00:04:36,665
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not about what you perceive.

70
00:04:37,126 --> 00:04:39,227
[SPEAKER_01]: Finding the better perception.

71
00:04:40,068 --> 00:04:41,989
[SPEAKER_01]: It's about understanding the nature of perception.

72
00:04:42,109 --> 00:04:48,733
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, whether it's agreeable, disagreeable or neither, agreeable or disagreeable, you'll be equanimous in regard to it.

73
00:04:49,113 --> 00:04:52,976
[SPEAKER_01]: Because there is no engagement with it of any kind.

74
00:04:54,997 --> 00:04:58,219
[SPEAKER_00]: It says, it talks, speaks about the ceka.

75
00:04:59,143 --> 00:05:01,864
[SPEAKER_00]: And how Ananda is one, a disciple in higher training.

76
00:05:02,104 --> 00:05:02,304
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

77
00:05:03,285 --> 00:05:04,865
[SPEAKER_00]: One who has entered upon the way.

78
00:05:06,886 --> 00:05:10,548
[SPEAKER_00]: Which may make you think, oh, no, he's a sotāpanna.

79
00:05:10,808 --> 00:05:12,008
[SPEAKER_00]: He's talking about a sotāpanna here.

80
00:05:12,269 --> 00:05:12,469
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

81
00:05:13,069 --> 00:05:15,090
[SPEAKER_00]: One in, one, a disciple in higher training.

82
00:05:15,110 --> 00:05:17,591
[SPEAKER_01]: He was already talking, he was already talking about sotāpanna before.

83
00:05:17,771 --> 00:05:17,931
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

84
00:05:17,951 --> 00:05:19,812
[SPEAKER_00]: But one who has entered upon the way.

85
00:05:20,112 --> 00:05:24,934
[SPEAKER_00]: So, to me, it sounds one who is actually a sotāpanna who is making efforts.

86
00:05:24,954 --> 00:05:25,334
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

87
00:05:25,454 --> 00:05:27,055
[SPEAKER_01]: Who is on the way to nibbāna, exactly.

88
00:05:27,095 --> 00:05:27,295
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

89
00:05:28,261 --> 00:05:38,709
[SPEAKER_01]: Because one can have the perception of an arahant, again, like what Mūla Parīyā Sūtra describes, but he hasn't fully developed that very understanding of that perception.

90
00:05:39,790 --> 00:05:42,272
[SPEAKER_01]: When I say I have a perception of an arahant, it means understanding the perception.

91
00:05:42,292 --> 00:05:49,037
[SPEAKER_01]: Like when he says he perceives earth, patujana, but then ārya-sāvaka, he knows, he directly knows earth.

92
00:05:50,799 --> 00:05:53,621
[SPEAKER_01]: He directly knows what he perceives, as in he understood the root of it.

93
00:05:54,061 --> 00:05:55,823
[SPEAKER_01]: He understood it as determined.

94
00:05:57,160 --> 00:06:02,943
[SPEAKER_01]: But, he might not now make further effort to speed up the results of that.

95
00:06:05,845 --> 00:06:13,549
[SPEAKER_01]: But the one who does make the effort, who entered upon the way, who is basically partaking in nibbāna actively, through his efforts, that's the next one.

96
00:06:14,690 --> 00:06:21,434
[SPEAKER_00]: And then he says, here and under, when a bhikkhu, the disciple in higher training, sees a form of the eye, hears a sound, smells,

97
00:06:22,448 --> 00:06:24,328
[SPEAKER_00]: That's how you develop nibbāna in this very life.

98
00:06:49,472 --> 00:06:50,713
[SPEAKER_01]: So, first, you need to see it.

99
00:06:51,353 --> 00:06:52,133
[SPEAKER_01]: You need to surmount it.

100
00:06:52,153 --> 00:06:53,274
[SPEAKER_01]: You need to see it as arisen.

101
00:06:54,855 --> 00:06:56,756
[SPEAKER_01]: As in, as determined not to do it with you.

102
00:06:57,116 --> 00:06:59,097
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's already peace.

103
00:06:59,538 --> 00:06:59,798
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

104
00:07:00,338 --> 00:07:00,978
[SPEAKER_01]: This is peace.

105
00:07:00,998 --> 00:07:01,178
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

106
00:07:01,219 --> 00:07:04,000
[SPEAKER_01]: That's, that's what differentiates Sotāpanna from, from Bhutujana.

107
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:07,302
[SPEAKER_01]: But then... Bhutujana would not have that peace of any kind.

108
00:07:08,018 --> 00:07:15,841
[SPEAKER_01]: Whether it's agreeable, disagreeable, he has no independent high ground on which he can stand peacefully and safely.

109
00:07:15,961 --> 00:07:16,722
[SPEAKER_01]: Sotāpanna has that.

110
00:07:17,282 --> 00:07:20,203
[SPEAKER_01]: But, these things will still keep arising for the duration of his life.

111
00:07:21,223 --> 00:07:23,424
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, the symptoms of the illness will still keep resisting.

112
00:07:23,804 --> 00:07:29,807
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if he wants to get rid of all of it, then he makes that higher training and higher virtue effort.

113
00:07:30,451 --> 00:07:38,635
[SPEAKER_01]: Whereby, even that peace that he has, in regard to agreeable, disagreeable, he starts regarding it as, no, this is all not wanted.

114
00:07:39,355 --> 00:07:40,356
[SPEAKER_01]: This is all determined.

115
00:07:40,656 --> 00:07:42,036
[SPEAKER_01]: He developed this passion towards it.

116
00:07:42,056 --> 00:07:49,240
[SPEAKER_01]: That's when Sariputta said you should regard pleasure as pain and pain as a deadly arrow.

117
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:52,881
[SPEAKER_01]: As in, like, so it's it's no more like pleasure and pain.

118
00:07:53,302 --> 00:07:55,322
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just pain and more pain.

119
00:07:57,664 --> 00:07:58,684
[SPEAKER_01]: As in, it's all disagreeable.

120
00:07:58,987 --> 00:08:08,495
[SPEAKER_01]: So, just to make sure you have uprooted the slightest sort of traces of ignorance that has manifested to some subtle lusts and whatnot.

121
00:08:09,475 --> 00:08:11,557
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's how even anāgāmī will become an arahant.

122
00:08:12,678 --> 00:08:19,904
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you take that as a blanket attitude that will then have to result in nibbāna for somebody who has the right view.

123
00:08:22,632 --> 00:08:27,354
[SPEAKER_01]: Again, like taking a broad spectrum antibiotics, they will have to get rid of this.

124
00:08:27,714 --> 00:08:28,855
[SPEAKER_01]: You're cured from the illness.

125
00:08:29,195 --> 00:08:29,655
[SPEAKER_01]: You're done.

126
00:08:29,695 --> 00:08:37,058
[SPEAKER_01]: You just need to wait and the body immune system will eventually make all the bacteria, whatever else is still flowing around, disappear.

127
00:08:37,739 --> 00:08:47,463
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, you take the strong medicine that you know works exactly right under the right conditions, you make that effort and you completely rid of any symptoms here and now as well.

128
00:08:51,310 --> 00:09:03,359
[SPEAKER_01]: But, again, without the right view, without having developed the sign of the mind, without having went through the existential solitude by yourself, without distraction and breaking of the virtue, to arrive at it, that's impossible.

129
00:09:06,341 --> 00:09:16,449
[SPEAKER_01]: That's also how, like, sometimes, you know, people might struggle to understand, but from Bhattacharya's point of view, sotāpanna is almost seen like an arahant, in a way.

130
00:09:18,290 --> 00:09:20,312
[SPEAKER_01]: And the difference is exactly in that.

131
00:09:21,289 --> 00:09:31,439
[SPEAKER_01]: There is a tremendous amount of peace that Sotāpanna already develops, by being free from illness, or in this case, by being equanimous in regard to agreeable, disagreeable or neutral.

132
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:34,882
[SPEAKER_01]: So, from Bhutujana's point of view, yeah, that's massive.

133
00:09:35,522 --> 00:09:43,770
[SPEAKER_01]: But now, from Arahant's point of view, even that, he can actually abandon, through development of that higher training.

134
00:09:44,871 --> 00:09:45,212
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

135
00:09:46,190 --> 00:09:50,093
[SPEAKER_01]: Through developing dispassion towards it, by seeing it all disagreeable.

136
00:09:50,113 --> 00:09:50,753
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly, yeah.

137
00:09:51,353 --> 00:09:57,557
[SPEAKER_01]: But... and that's also... that's... that's how you can also understand why sometimes sotāpānas would need encouragement from the Buddha.

138
00:09:57,577 --> 00:10:00,739
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, again, people often think, oh, it's automatic.

139
00:10:00,839 --> 00:10:04,902
[SPEAKER_01]: Right view, nibbāna, arahantship is just like automatic process or something.

140
00:10:04,962 --> 00:10:05,362
[SPEAKER_01]: It isn't.

141
00:10:07,323 --> 00:10:12,487
[SPEAKER_01]: Person who has become a sotāpāna, in this case, developed that equanimity in regard to whatever touches him,

142
00:10:15,639 --> 00:10:17,881
[SPEAKER_01]: He doesn't get struck by the second arrow of suffering.

143
00:10:18,401 --> 00:10:21,484
[SPEAKER_01]: So, he doesn't suffer anymore from that point of equanimity.

144
00:10:21,864 --> 00:10:26,008
[SPEAKER_01]: Even when suffering arises, he doesn't suffer amidst suffering.

145
00:10:28,130 --> 00:10:29,651
[SPEAKER_01]: Many people will be content with that.

146
00:10:30,031 --> 00:10:31,613
[SPEAKER_01]: Many sotāpannas will be content with that.

147
00:10:32,303 --> 00:10:34,224
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's already a tremendous amount of freedom.

148
00:10:34,904 --> 00:10:42,886
[SPEAKER_01]: And, like, from the... from the previous standpoint, all the symptoms, lingering symptoms, occasional annoyances and so on, it's nothing.

149
00:10:43,126 --> 00:10:43,686
[SPEAKER_01]: It's trifle.

150
00:10:43,746 --> 00:10:44,026
[SPEAKER_01]: Nothing.

151
00:10:45,587 --> 00:10:46,087
[SPEAKER_00]: Nothing left.

152
00:10:46,747 --> 00:10:47,007
[SPEAKER_01]: Really.

153
00:10:47,247 --> 00:10:50,368
[SPEAKER_01]: In that... from that... and that's... that's the symbol of seven grains and Himalayas.

154
00:10:50,448 --> 00:10:51,448
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how little is left.

155
00:10:51,468 --> 00:10:52,469
[SPEAKER_01]: There's nothing left, really.

156
00:10:53,609 --> 00:10:56,670
[SPEAKER_01]: But was it what... even that seven grains is still something left.

157
00:10:58,362 --> 00:11:05,785
[SPEAKER_01]: So, although you're already equanimous in regard to pain, pleasure and neutral, you should make the effort and develop this passion to adopt it.

158
00:11:07,746 --> 00:11:12,809
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's how you set up on the way of the higher training that results in nibbāna, here and now.

159
00:11:14,710 --> 00:11:17,971
[SPEAKER_01]: And again, that's how sometimes they didn't do it.

160
00:11:17,991 --> 00:11:20,852
[SPEAKER_01]: Sometimes sotāpanna stays content with it.

161
00:11:20,872 --> 00:11:25,955
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, even Venerable Ananda, living by the Buddha, with the Buddha for like, I don't know, 20 years, he's attended this.

162
00:11:26,887 --> 00:11:28,248
[SPEAKER_01]: He was perfectly content.

163
00:11:28,328 --> 00:11:32,130
[SPEAKER_01]: And it doesn't mean that he was, you know, he was quite peaceful most of the time, probably.

164
00:11:33,211 --> 00:11:37,894
[SPEAKER_01]: Only when, like, Sariputta died, that he was sort of got in mind, got clouded and so on.

165
00:11:38,234 --> 00:11:46,279
[SPEAKER_01]: But even that, he might have lost, like, his faculties might have kind of got, he lost the clarity of it.

166
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:50,322
[SPEAKER_01]: But what he still couldn't lose is that high ground of equanimity, of safety.

167
00:11:51,791 --> 00:11:54,974
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, all you need to do is just, when that phenomenon ceases, it's all there.

168
00:11:55,355 --> 00:11:58,358
[SPEAKER_01]: So, he hasn't been suffering, even amidst the suffering.

169
00:11:58,978 --> 00:12:01,441
[SPEAKER_01]: Vāpatujana would be completely distraught and overwhelmed.

170
00:12:02,342 --> 00:12:08,929
[SPEAKER_01]: But, from Arahant's point of view, there is still a degree to be achieved.

171
00:12:11,025 --> 00:12:21,650
[SPEAKER_01]: And you do so by regarding even those states of, okay, I'm, you know, agreeable can't touch me, disagreeable can't touch me, neither agreeable, neither disagreeable can touch me, and now that shouldn't touch me either.

172
00:12:23,791 --> 00:12:28,114
[SPEAKER_01]: You develop attitude towards that as disagreeable, as not wanted.

173
00:12:28,474 --> 00:12:32,536
[SPEAKER_01]: So you really, through and through, practice that disenchantment.

174
00:12:36,355 --> 00:12:43,821
[SPEAKER_00]: And he goes on to describe the arahant, and how Ananda is one, a noble one, with developed faculties.

175
00:12:45,402 --> 00:12:46,963
[SPEAKER_00]: This is a bit of a tongue twister.

176
00:12:49,165 --> 00:12:53,388
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you hear Ananda when a bhikkhu sees a form with the eye, hears a sound with the ear, and so on.

177
00:12:55,750 --> 00:12:58,092
[SPEAKER_00]: There arises in him what is agreeable,

178
00:12:59,375 --> 00:13:00,096
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he's arahant.

179
00:13:00,936 --> 00:13:02,878
[SPEAKER_00]: There arises what is agreeable, what is disagreeable.

180
00:13:03,218 --> 00:13:05,319
[SPEAKER_00]: There arises what is both agreeable and disagreeable.

181
00:13:05,459 --> 00:13:06,480
[SPEAKER_01]: Same like for all three.

182
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:11,123
[SPEAKER_01]: So, he's not, like, oblivious to what's in front of him, as in robotic.

183
00:13:11,263 --> 00:13:14,005
[SPEAKER_01]: He knows, oh, this is agreeable, this is disagreeable, this is neutral.

184
00:13:14,706 --> 00:13:15,907
[SPEAKER_01]: So, none of that has changed.

185
00:13:19,309 --> 00:13:24,453
[SPEAKER_00]: And then he says, if he should wish, may I abide perceiving the unrepulsive, then the repulsive.

186
00:13:25,153 --> 00:13:27,235
[SPEAKER_00]: He abides perceiving the unrepulsive, then the repulsive.

187
00:13:28,086 --> 00:13:34,308
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what I said.

188
00:13:34,888 --> 00:13:45,591
[SPEAKER_01]: If you develop it, that attitude, then agreeable will be seen as disagreeable, and disagreeable will be seen as twice as disagreeable.

189
00:13:47,472 --> 00:13:50,493
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you can perceive what is disagreeable and agreeable.

190
00:13:51,528 --> 00:14:02,971
[SPEAKER_01]: Or the agreeable and the disagreeable, as in it's less disagreeable on account of disagreeable, because you fully surmounted the whole domain of the determined, that which is determined as agreeable, disagreeable.

191
00:14:03,671 --> 00:14:07,172
[SPEAKER_01]: You see its basis, you see itself, you see that dhamma, you understand it.

192
00:14:07,812 --> 00:14:10,393
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yeah, if you wish to look at this aspect or that aspect, why?

193
00:14:10,713 --> 00:14:12,033
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you're completely free from it.

194
00:14:13,314 --> 00:14:14,634
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, it's a pleasant abiding.

195
00:14:14,934 --> 00:14:16,295
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah, completely.

196
00:14:16,535 --> 00:14:17,395
[SPEAKER_01]: It went beyond.

197
00:14:17,495 --> 00:14:17,635
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

198
00:14:18,428 --> 00:14:28,716
[SPEAKER_00]: Because if he should wish, may I avoid both repulsive and unrepulsive, abide in equanimity, mindful and fully aware.

199
00:14:28,916 --> 00:14:31,438
[SPEAKER_00]: He abides in equanimity, towards that, mindful and fully aware.

200
00:14:35,081 --> 00:14:39,845
[SPEAKER_01]: Repulsive and unrepulsive, it's basically really repulsive and slightly less repulsive.

201
00:14:43,697 --> 00:14:48,039
[SPEAKER_00]: And that is the supreme development of the faculties in the Noble One's discipline.

202
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:52,502
[SPEAKER_00]: And He goes and says, what should be done for His disciples?

203
00:14:52,542 --> 00:14:58,145
[SPEAKER_00]: What should be done for His disciples out of compassion by a teacher who seeks their welfare and has compassion for them?

204
00:14:58,385 --> 00:14:59,886
[SPEAKER_00]: That I have done for you, Ananda.

205
00:15:00,726 --> 00:15:03,688
[SPEAKER_00]: There are these roots of trees, these entrances.

206
00:15:03,768 --> 00:15:04,508
[SPEAKER_00]: Meditate.

207
00:15:04,888 --> 00:15:05,429
[SPEAKER_00]: Do not delay.

208
00:15:05,449 --> 00:15:05,949
[SPEAKER_00]: Contemplate.

209
00:15:06,529 --> 00:15:07,009
[SPEAKER_01]: Reflect.

210
00:15:08,410 --> 00:15:09,831
[SPEAKER_00]: Or else you will regret it later.

211
00:15:10,833 --> 00:15:13,298
[SPEAKER_01]: Go there, make the effort to understand the nature of things.

212
00:15:13,638 --> 00:15:16,083
[SPEAKER_01]: Don't go there, make the effort to look at your nostrils.

